# Line endings for files that BREAK when they carry CRLF, regardless of which
# OS commits them.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf on, so the working copy
# gets CRLF. Git normalises to LF in the object store, which is why Linux CI
# has worked so far -- but that is a property of each developer's local config,
# not of the repo, and it only takes one contributor with autocrlf=false to
# commit a shell script that fails on the VPS with:
#     /opt/aegislead/deploy.sh: bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M
# These rules make the LF guarantee belong to the repo instead.
#
# Scoped deliberately to executable/config formats. A blanket `* text=auto
# eol=lf` would rewrite every source file in the working tree on next
# checkout, which is a separate (and much larger) change -- and the right one
# to pair with fixing the ~2000 prettier CRLF lint errors.

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
Caddyfile   text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
